120\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{3}$ members."} :step/id #uuid "c2970b7a-793f-5b1c-9e78-4dd00bd3e750" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566289}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566316 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ec9087c-76ac-5207-b1f9-ec6fe4b81431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{9}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565729} {:answer/id #uuid "36010bc1-90bd-5d59-bf60-398650da4041" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{2}^{9}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565762} {:answer/id #uuid "6e47a032-29fd-5008-bafe-e0cc57a28e71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565852} {:answer/id #uuid "b130822a-20ed-52e4-9477-4de7e3cf757a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{2}^{9}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565957} {:answer/id #uuid "b7594013-bebf-56a0-a402-a6f6ee3a5b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{9}\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565979}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565979} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d943c3b-30bf-5f50-9d21-212a996b1fd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "09a2f783-f81f-5ba2-8e8b-78ad6330c2dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-61687" :question/problem "A radioactive substance decays exponentially such that its mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every hour. If the mass of the substance was initially $2\\,\\text{kg},$ what is the mass of the substance after $9$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "If the mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4},$ then $\\frac{3}{4}$ of its mass remains every hour.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ hour, the 